    {
        "content": "<p>If you use <code>set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false</code> it works,  for more information I think this could be helpful : <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Init/MetaTypes.html#Implicit-arguments-and-transparency\">implicit-arguments-and-transparency</a> . </p>\n<p>Basically it is a big change in how tactics work when there are implicit arguments (and your second proof avoids this  entirely as <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=PNat.factorMultiset_pow#doc\">docs#PNat.factorMultiset_pow</a> has no implicit arguments, and you don't use tactic mode on <code>count_nsmul</code> for the final <code>calc</code> line).</p>",
        "id": 582735891,
        "sender_full_name": "Yan Yablonovskiy 🇺🇦",
        "timestamp": 1774945197
    }
